      "config": {
        "displaySettings": {},
        "isSupportCustomProperty": false,
        "supportCustomProperty": false,
        "name": "PSC Executive Dashboard Guide - Read First",
        "description": "",
        "theme": "newSolidDarkBlue",
        "interval": 3,
        "type": "text",
        "timescale": "day",
        "version": 2,
        "content": "<section class=\"psc-exec-intro\"><style>\n.psc-exec-intro {\n  font-family: Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif;\n  background: linear-gradient(135deg, #0f172a 0%, #111827 45%, #1e3a8a 100%);\n  color: #ffffff;\n  border-radius: 16px;\n  padding: 22px;\n  box-sizing: border-box;\n  box-shadow: 0 8px 24px rgba(15, 23, 42, 0.32);\n}\n.psc-exec-header {\n  display: flex;\n  justify-content: space-between;\n  align-items: flex-start;\n  gap: 20px;\n  margin-bottom: 20px;\n}\n.psc-exec-title h1 {\n  margin: 0 0 7px 0;\n  font-size: 28px;\n  line-height: 1.15;\n  font-weight: 750;\n  letter-spacing: .2px;\n}\n.psc-exec-title p {\n  margin: 0;\n  max-width: 980px;\n  color: #dbeafe;\n  font-size: 14px;\n  line-height: 1.55;\n}\n.psc-exec-badge {\n  background: rgba(96, 165, 250, .18);\n  border: 1px solid rgba(191, 219, 254, .34);\n  border-radius: 999px;\n  padding: 9px 15px;\n  color: #eff6ff;\n  font-size: 13px;\n  font-weight: 700;\n  white-space: nowrap;\n}\n.psc-exec-grid {\n  display: grid;\n  grid-template-columns: repeat(4, minmax(0, 1fr));\n  gap: 14px;\n  margin-bottom: 16px;\n}\n.psc-exec-card {\n  background: rgba(15, 23, 42, .76);\n  border: 1px solid rgba(148, 163, 184, .34);\n  border-radius: 14px;\n  padding: 16px;\n  min-height: 150px;\n  box-sizing: border-box;\n}\n.psc-exec-card h3 {\n  margin: 0 0 8px 0;\n  font-size: 15px;\n  color: #ffffff;\n}\n.psc-exec-card p {\n  margin: 0;\n  font-size: 13px;\n  line-height: 1.48;\n  color: #cbd5e1;\n}\n.psc-exec-icon {\n  width: 50px;\n  height: 32px;\n  border-radius: 11px;\n  background: rgba(59, 130, 246, .22);\n  border: 1px solid rgba(255, 255, 255, .18);\n  display: flex;\n  align-items: center;\n  justify-content: center;\n  margin-bottom: 12px;\n  font-size: 11px;\n  font-weight: 800;\n  letter-spacing: .8px;\n  color: #dbeafe;\n}\n.psc-exec-action {\n  display: inline-block;\n  margin-top: 12px;\n  padding: 7px 11px;\n  border-radius: 999px;\n  background: rgba(255, 255, 255, .12);\n  border: 1px solid rgba(255, 255, 255, .18);\n  color: #bfdbfe;\n  font-size: 12px;\n  font-weight: 700;\n}\n.psc-exec-footer {\n  display: grid;\n  grid-template-columns: 1.2fr 1fr;\n  gap: 14px;\n  margin-top: 14px;\n}\n.psc-exec-panel {\n  background: rgba(255, 255, 255, .08);\n  border: 1px solid rgba(255, 255, 255, .14);\n  border-radius: 14px;\n  padding: 16px;\n}\n.psc-exec-panel h3 {\n  margin: 0 0 10px 0;\n  font-size: 15px;\n  color: #ffffff;\n}\n.psc-exec-panel ul {\n  margin: 0;\n  padding-left: 18px;\n  color: #dbeafe;\n  font-size: 13px;\n  line-height: 1.62;\n}\n.psc-exec-note {\n  font-size: 13px;\n  line-height: 1.5;\n  color: #dbeafe;\n  margin: 0;\n}\n.psc-scope-row {\n  display: flex;\n  gap: 8px;\n  flex-wrap: wrap;\n  margin-top: 11px;\n}\n.psc-scope-pill {\n  border-radius: 999px;\n  padding: 6px 10px;\n  font-size: 12px;\n  font-weight: 700;\n  border: 1px solid rgba(255, 255, 255, .18);\n}\n.scope-health { background: rgba(22, 163, 74, .92); color: #ecfdf5; }\n.scope-alerts { background: rgba(239, 68, 68, .92); color: #fff7ed; }\n.scope-region { background: rgba(59, 130, 246, .9); color: #eff6ff; }\n.scope-sites { background: rgba(14, 165, 233, .9); color: #082f49; }\n.scope-capacity { background: rgba(250, 204, 21, .9); color: #422006; }\n.scope-sessions { background: rgba(168, 85, 247, .88); color: #faf5ff; }\n@media (max-width: 1100px) {\n  .psc-exec-grid { grid-template-columns: repeat(2, minmax(0, 1fr)); }\n}\n@media (max-width: 800px) {\n  .psc-exec-header, .psc-exec-footer { grid-template-columns: 1fr; display: block; }\n  .psc-exec-grid { grid-template-columns: 1fr; }\n  .psc-exec-badge { display: inline-block; margin-top: 12px; }\n  .psc-exec-panel { margin-top: 14px; }\n}\n</style>\n<div class=\"psc-exec-header\">\n  <div class=\"psc-exec-title\">\n    <h1>PSC Network Health Executive Command Center</h1>\n    <p>This dashboard is the executive landing page for PSC network health. It is designed to answer five questions quickly: Are we healthy? Which regions are impacted? Are active exceptions business-impacting? Are acquisitions or special programs at risk? Do Fortibranch capacity trends require action?</p>\n  </div>\n  <div class=\"psc-exec-badge\">Executive Network Operations View</div>\n</div>\n<div class=\"psc-exec-grid\">\n  <div class=\"psc-exec-card\">\n    <div class=\"psc-exec-icon\">START</div>\n    <h3>Start with regional health</h3>\n    <p>Use <b>Executive Health by Region</b> to identify whether issues are isolated to one region or spread across the PSC estate.</p>\n    <span class=\"psc-exec-action\">Review: Executive Health by Region</span>\n  </div>\n  <div class=\"psc-exec-card\">\n    <div class=\"psc-exec-icon\">MAP</div>\n    <h3>Locate geographic impact</h3>\n    <p>Use <b>PSC Geographic Impact</b> to understand where impacted PSC resources are located and whether the issue has geographic concentration.</p>\n    <span class=\"psc-exec-action\">Review: PSC Geographic Impact</span>\n  </div>\n  <div class=\"psc-exec-card\">\n    <div class=\"psc-exec-icon\">EXC</div>\n    <h3>Confirm active exceptions</h3>\n    <p>Use <b>Executive Network Exceptions</b> for active alerts, affected resource, datapoint, value, and ServiceNow ticket visibility.</p>\n    <span class=\"psc-exec-action\">Review: Executive Exceptions</span>\n  </div>\n  <div class=\"psc-exec-card\">\n    <div class=\"psc-exec-icon\">CAP</div>\n    <h3>Validate capacity risk</h3>\n    <p>Use the Fortibranch capacity section to review active sessions, CPU, memory, and disk pressure before the issue becomes service-impacting.</p>\n    <span class=\"psc-exec-action\">Review: Capacity Risk</span>\n  </div>\n  <div class=\"psc-exec-card\">\n    <div class=\"psc-exec-icon\">SITE</div>\n    <h3>Check acquisitions</h3>\n    <p>Use <b>Acquisition / Special Program Health</b> for Dexter, Karsner, Polaris, and other watched programs that require executive visibility.</p>\n    <span class=\"psc-exec-action\">Review: Acquisition Health</span>\n  </div>\n  <div class=\"psc-exec-card\">\n    <div class=\"psc-exec-icon\">NOC</div>\n    <h3>Use the status board</h3>\n    <p>The NOC-style status board provides a fast operational signal by resource group without forcing executives to review every region tile.</p>\n    <span class=\"psc-exec-action\">Review: PSC Status Board</span>\n  </div>\n  <div class=\"psc-exec-card\">\n    <div class=\"psc-exec-icon\">FLOW</div>\n    <h3>Drill down only when needed</h3>\n    <p>Open the regional or acquisition detail dashboards only when this page shows a red/yellow signal, abnormal trend, or business exception.</p>\n    <span class=\"psc-exec-action\">Use dashboard group menu</span>\n  </div>\n  <div class=\"psc-exec-card\">\n    <div class=\"psc-exec-icon\">TEAM</div>\n    <h3>Team review behavior</h3>\n    <p>Executives should review the top half; operations should use the exception, status board, and capacity widgets to determine next action.</p>\n    <span class=\"psc-exec-action\">Review top to bottom</span>\n  </div>\n</div>\n<div class=\"psc-exec-footer\">\n  <div class=\"psc-exec-panel\">\n    <h3>Recommended Review Flow</h3>\n    <ul>\n      <li>Start with the KPI strip to confirm PSC scope and monitored coverage.</li>\n      <li>Review regional health and the map to determine business or geographic impact.</li>\n      <li>Use active exceptions to confirm severity, affected resource, datapoint, value, ticket status, and SDT context.</li>\n      <li>Review acquisition and Fortibranch capacity sections when an exception requires operational follow-up.</li>\n      <li>Use the dashboard group menu for regional drill-down dashboards such as West, North, East, Southwest, Great Midwest, Southeast, and Acquisitions.</li>\n    </ul>\n  </div>\n  <div class=\"psc-exec-panel\">\n    <h3>Dashboard Scope</h3>\n    <p class=\"psc-exec-note\">This view is intentionally executive-first: it highlights health, exceptions, geographic impact, and capacity risk. Detailed per-region NOC and map widgets should live in supporting drill-down dashboards, not on this landing page.</p>\n    <div class=\"psc-scope-row\">\n      <span class=\"psc-scope-pill scope-health\">Health</span>\n      <span class=\"psc-scope-pill scope-alerts\">Alerts</span>\n      <span class=\"psc-scope-pill scope-region\">Regions</span>\n      <span class=\"psc-scope-pill scope-sites\">Acquisitions</span>\n      <span class=\"psc-scope-pill scope-capacity\">Capacity</span>\n      <span class=\"psc-scope-pill scope-sessions\">Sessions</span>\n    </div>\n  </div>\n</div>\n</section>"
      }
    },
